-- Generated by `pnpm decisions:seed` from docs/planning/decisions.md (decision 191): the log's
-- entries as decisions, numbered as in the log, active unless a later entry replaces them.
-- Do not edit by hand.
insert into public.decisions
  (number, statement, reason, status, decided_by_name, decided_at, origin, origin_ref)
overriding system value
values
  (209, 'Changes to slice 3.2 after an independent review, before it merged. A replacement of an active decision skips the wait only when it would be active anyway, which proves its decider is the asker, and that person is one of the replaced decision''s deciders; who the model names as deciding is never trusted on its own. A replacement found by listening always waits. An area''s owner decides a replacement only if they owned the area when the replaced decision was made; otherwise the fallback does. A conflict that names decisions is decided by those decisions'' areas, and an area the teammate names that differs is refused. A tool call answered again answers from what it recorded, and its post is rebuilt from the stored deciders. A conflict recorded with nobody to decide it is decided by the fallback configured now. A conflict''s area is the replaced decision''s. Left as they are: decisions are looked up by number across workspaces, which matters only once there is more than one (wave 5), and proposals recorded before this change are not guarded after it', 'The review showed that any writer in a thread could replace someone else''s decision by having the call name a decider who had written there, that listening could do the same, that making oneself owner of an area made one''s own replacement active at once, and that the teammate could pick which owner decided a conflict. Each now has a test', 'active', 'the owner', '2026-11-25T00:00:00Z', 'import', '209')
on conflict (origin, origin_ref) where origin_ref is not null do nothing;
